# Clean URLs for a single-page site, added 2026-09-23.
#
# WHY. bugit.dev routes entirely through hash fragments (/#pricing, /#/docs/privacy). A hash is
# never sent to the server, so every address a person would actually type, paste, link or cite
# answered 404. Measured on 2026-09-23 against production, seventeen of seventeen obvious entry
# points failed: /pricing /features /docs /download /privacy /terms /faq /support /contact
# /changelog /blog /integrations /ja/ /de/ /en/ /legal /security. Two of those are the legal
# surfaces a customer or a regulator is most likely to try by hand.
#
# WHY 302 AND NOT 301. A 301 is cached hard by browsers and is effectively permanent; these
# mappings have never run in production. Nothing is lost by starting reversible: every
# destination is a hash route on this same origin, and every hash route already canonicalises
# to https://bugit.dev/, so there is no link equity for a 301 to consolidate that a 302 would
# forfeit. Promote these to 301 once they have been observed working, not before.
#
# A DESTINATION HERE IS A CLAIM THAT A ROUTE EXISTS. `docRoutes` in app.js is the authority for
# the /#/... targets and the section ids in index.html are the authority for the /#... ones.
# scripts/check-seo.mjs reads both and fails if any destination below has stopped existing,
# because a redirect that quietly points at a renamed route is worse than the 404 it replaced:
# it answers 200 and shows the wrong page.
#
# `#` is a comment only at the start of a line in this format, so the fragments below parse.
# Cloudflare's own documented example is `/page/ /page2/#fragment 301`.

# --- homepage sections -------------------------------------------------------
/pricing          /#pricing             302
/features         /#features            302
/integrations     /#integrations        302
/faq              /#faq                 302
/demo             /#demo                302
/download         /#pricing             302

# --- documentation -----------------------------------------------------------
/docs             /#/docs               302
/documentation    /#/docs               302
/legal            /#/docs               302
/guide            /#/docs/user-guide    302
/user-guide       /#/docs/user-guide    302
/getting-started  /#/docs/user-guide    302
/overview         /#/docs/overview      302

# --- legal surfaces ----------------------------------------------------------
# The four a customer or a regulator types by hand. /terms and /eula both resolve to the licence
# agreement because that is the document this product actually publishes under those names.
/privacy          /#/docs/privacy       302
/privacy-policy   /#/docs/privacy       302
/terms            /#/docs/license       302
/eula             /#/docs/license       302
/license          /#/docs/license       302
/licence          /#/docs/license       302
/refund           /#/docs/refund        302
/refunds          /#/docs/refund        302
/commerce         /#/docs/commerce      302

# --- support -----------------------------------------------------------------
/support          /#/support            302
/contact          /#/support            302
/help             /#/support            302
